Shared CRE entrypoint / identity / Envelope branches live in CREReceiverBase.tree.
This tree covers only the strategy-specific report handling, views, and policy knobs.

CREStrategyExecutor::constructor(address registry_, address forwarder_, uint64 chainSelector_, uint64 maxReportAge_)
└── Given the base constructor succeeds
    ├── It should set minDepositETH = 0.1 ether
    ├── It should set minWithdrawETH = 0.01 ether
    ├── It should set minHarvestETH = 0.01 ether
    ├── It should set syncInterval = 1 days and lastSyncAt = block.timestamp
    ├── It should set minExitLiquidityTopUpETH = 0.01 ether
    ├── It should leave controllerReserveETH and exitLiquidityTargetETH at 0 (explicit
    │   deploy-time policy knobs — 0 disables the exit-liquidity action entirely)
    └── It should report version() == "1.0.0-cre"

CREStrategyExecutor::_processReport(uint8 action, bytes params) — via onReport
├── It should ignore params entirely: every ETH amount is recomputed from live
│   Controller / StrategyManager / ExitQueue / AMM state before any call
├── Given action decodes to an out-of-range StrategyAction value
│   └── It should revert (enum conversion panic before any protocol call)
├── Given action is StrategyAction.None
│   └── It should revert with KeeperExecutorUnknownAction
├── Given action is StrategyAction.Rebalance
│   ├── When no registered strategy is both unpaused and unhealthy
│   │   └── It should revert with KeeperExecutorNoUpkeepNeeded
│   └── When at least one unpaused strategy reports isHealthy() == false
│       ├── It should call Controller.checkAndRebalanceStrategies()
│       └── It should emit StrategyUpkeepPerformed(Rebalance, 0)
├── Given action is StrategyAction.WithdrawShortfall
│   ├── When pending redemption needs are already covered by the Controller balance
│   │   └── It should revert with KeeperExecutorNoUpkeepNeeded
│   ├── When the shortfall is below minWithdrawETH
│   │   └── It should revert with KeeperExecutorNoUpkeepNeeded (dust guard)
│   └── When the shortfall is at least minWithdrawETH
│       ├── It should call Controller.withdrawFromStrategies(shortfall) with the recomputed
│       │   amount, not any amount from the report
│       └── It should emit StrategyUpkeepPerformed(WithdrawShortfall, shortfall)
├── Given action is StrategyAction.ProvideExitLiquidity
│   ├── When exitLiquidityTargetETH is 0
│   │   └── It should revert with KeeperExecutorNoUpkeepNeeded (action disabled by policy)
│   ├── When AMM.freeBalance() already meets the target
│   │   └── It should revert with KeeperExecutorNoUpkeepNeeded
│   ├── When the computed top-up is below minExitLiquidityTopUpETH
│   │   └── It should revert with KeeperExecutorNoUpkeepNeeded
│   └── When the top-up is at least minExitLiquidityTopUpETH
│       ├── It should top up by min(target shortfall, idle Controller excess) — never
│       │   spending the controllerReserveETH or the ETH earmarked for pending redemptions
│       ├── It should call Controller.provideExitLiquidity(topUp)
│       └── It should emit StrategyUpkeepPerformed(ProvideExitLiquidity, topUp)
├── Given action is StrategyAction.DepositExcess
│   ├── When idle excess is below minDepositETH
│   │   └── It should revert with KeeperExecutorNoUpkeepNeeded
│   ├── When no strategy can currently take a deposit (all paused, unhealthy, in deposit
│   │   cooldown, or at maxDeposit == 0)
│   │   └── It should revert with KeeperExecutorNoUpkeepNeeded
│   └── When excess >= minDepositETH and some strategy has capacity
│       ├── It should deposit only the excess over controllerReserveETH + pending needs
│       ├── It should call Controller.depositToStrategies(excess)
│       └── It should emit StrategyUpkeepPerformed(DepositExcess, excess)
├── Given action is StrategyAction.HarvestPerformanceFees
│   ├── When StrategyManager.performanceFeeBps() == 0
│   │   └── It should revert with KeeperExecutorNoUpkeepNeeded (fees disabled ⇒ pending is 0)
│   ├── When total pending fee ETH is below minHarvestETH
│   │   └── It should revert with KeeperExecutorNoUpkeepNeeded (harvest not worth the gas)
│   └── When total pending fee ETH is at least minHarvestETH
│       ├── It should call Controller.harvestPerformanceFeeFromStrategies()
│       └── It should emit StrategyUpkeepPerformed(HarvestPerformanceFees, feeETH)
└── Given action is StrategyAction.Sync
    ├── When syncInterval is 0
    │   └── It should revert with KeeperExecutorNoUpkeepNeeded (sync disabled)
    ├── When block.timestamp - lastSyncAt < syncInterval
    │   └── It should revert with KeeperExecutorNoUpkeepNeeded (rate limit)
    └── When the interval has elapsed
        ├── It should set lastSyncAt = block.timestamp BEFORE calling out
        ├── It should call Controller.syncStrategies()
        └── It should emit StrategyUpkeepPerformed(Sync, 0)

CREStrategyExecutor::strategyUpkeepStatus()
├── Given the executor itself is paused
│   └── It should return (None, 0)
├── Given Controller or StrategyManager is paused
│   └── It should return (None, 0)
└── Given nothing is paused, it should return the FIRST applicable action in priority order
    ├── Rebalance (an unhealthy unpaused strategy outranks everything — it is the only
    │   action that repairs the NAV source)
    ├── WithdrawShortfall — additionally requires total maxWithdrawal() > 0, so it is never
    │   recommended when no strategy can actually pay out
    ├── ProvideExitLiquidity
    ├── DepositExcess
    ├── HarvestPerformanceFees
    ├── Sync — additionally requires strategyCount() > 0
    └── None when no threshold is met
    └── It should agree with _processReport: any action this view returns must not revert
        with KeeperExecutorNoUpkeepNeeded in the same block

CREStrategyExecutor::pendingRedemptionNeedsETH()
├── It should anchor the scan at CREQueueExecutor.nextLiveBatchIdToProcess() (the two
│   executors share one cursor; the queue executor owns it)
├── It should scan at most MAX_BATCH_SCAN (25) batches — gas-bounded
├── Given a scanned batch is not priced
│   └── It should contribute 0
├── Given a scanned batch is past MAX_BATCH_PROCESSING_TIME
│   └── It should contribute 0 (users self-serve via the escape hatch; do not reserve ETH)
├── Given a request is slippage-protected out
│   └── It should contribute 0 for that request
├── Given a batch has more unprocessed users than MAX_USERS_COST_SCAN (50)
│   └── It should cost at most the first 50 (may under-report; the shortfall is topped up on
│       the next upkeep rather than reverting)
└── It should always add the current batch's totalTokensToBurn priced at
    AMM.eveBasePriceInETH() — the batch is not yet priced (cancellable equity);
    the live base price is already net of in-window priced liability

CREStrategyExecutor::setControllerReserveETH / setExitLiquidityTargetETH / setSyncInterval / setMinWithdrawETH
├── Given caller does not have ADMIN_ROLE
│   └── It should revert with RegistryClientMissingRole
└── Given caller has ADMIN_ROLE
    ├── It should accept 0 as an explicit, meaningful choice (no reserve / action disabled /
    │   sync disabled / no dust floor)
    ├── It should emit the matching *Changed(old, new) event
    └── It should store the new value

CREStrategyExecutor::setMinDepositETH / setMinHarvestETH / setMinExitLiquidityTopUpETH
├── Given caller does not have ADMIN_ROLE
│   └── It should revert with RegistryClientMissingRole
├── Given the new value is 0
│   └── It should revert with KeeperExecutorInvalidConfig — these are dust floors; zeroing
│       them would let a workflow burn gas on economically pointless upkeeps
└── Given caller has ADMIN_ROLE and the value is non-zero
    ├── It should emit the matching *Changed(old, new) event
    └── It should store the new value
